F. Data checks

F1. Date and timestamp ranges (finds bad dates that SQL Server may reject)

sql
SELECT c.table_name, c.column_name, c.data_type,
  extractvalue(xmltype(dbms_xmlgen.getxml(
    'select to_char(min("'||c.column_name||'"),''YYYY-MM-DD'') mn from "'||c.table_name||'"')),'/ROWSET/ROW/MN') AS min_date,
  extractvalue(xmltype(dbms_xmlgen.getxml(
    'select to_char(max("'||c.column_name||'"),''YYYY-MM-DD'') mx from "'||c.table_name||'"')),'/ROWSET/ROW/MX') AS max_date
FROM user_tab_columns c
JOIN user_tables t ON t.table_name = c.table_name
WHERE c.data_type = 'DATE' OR c.data_type LIKE 'TIMESTAMP%'
ORDER BY c.table_name, c.column_name;

F2. Real scale and precision of NUMBER columns without declared precision

sql
SELECT c.table_name, c.column_name,
  extractvalue(xmltype(dbms_xmlgen.getxml(
    'select max(case when instr(to_char("'||c.column_name||'",''TM9''),''.'')>0 then length(to_char("'||c.column_name||'",''TM9''))-instr(to_char("'||c.column_name||'",''TM9''),''.'') else 0 end) ms from "'||c.table_name||'"')),'/ROWSET/ROW/MS') AS max_decimal_places,
  extractvalue(xmltype(dbms_xmlgen.getxml(
    'select max(length(replace(replace(to_char(abs("'||c.column_name||'"),''TM9''),''.'',''''),''E'',''''))) md from "'||c.table_name||'"')),'/ROWSET/ROW/MD') AS max_digits
FROM user_tab_columns c
JOIN user_tables t ON t.table_name = c.table_name
WHERE c.data_type = 'NUMBER' AND c.data_precision IS NULL
ORDER BY c.table_name, c.column_name;

This tells me whether each of those columns can safely become int, bigint, or decimal(p,s). If it returns nothing, there are no such columns.

